.nh
.TH "PB-MACHINE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-machine - Manage machines


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb machine [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List and manage the machines enrolled in your account: print the command that enrolls a new
one (add), rename it, choose whether it may sleep (availability), choose which incoming services
it accepts (capabilities), tag it, or revoke it. These commands name any enrolled machine by name
or ID; pb setup is what configures the machine you are sitting at. Revoking disconnects the
enrollment, it does not just hide the machine from the list.

.PP
In an interactive terminal, pb machine with no subcommand opens the machine picker. Elsewhere it
prints this help.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for machine


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb machine list
  pb machine add --name db-1
  pb machine revoke old-laptop
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP, \fBpb-machine-add(1)\fP, \fBpb-machine-availability(1)\fP, \fBpb-machine-capabilities(1)\fP, \fBpb-machine-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-machine-rename(1)\fP, \fBpb-machine-revoke(1)\fP, \fBpb-machine-tag(1)\fP
